// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5958 new: Browser External Extensions Silent Install Detection (Windows, macOS, Linux)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5958
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Suspicious Browser External Extension Registration on Windows
// Sigma ID: 51f077e1-9126-4c9a-a834-8998f8a8d93b
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001
// Description: Detects the creation of registry entries used to register external browser extensions on
//   Windows. External extensions can be installed from external update URLs without user interaction
//   by writing to the Extensions registry key with an update_url value. Adversaries may abuse this
//   to silently install malicious browser extensions across reboots.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate software installers registering browser extensions (password managers, screen readers, etc.)
//   - Enterprise IT administrators deploying browser extensions
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/extensions/developer-guide/alternate-distribution-options
//   - https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/chrome/common/chrome_paths.cc
//   - https://github.com/praetorian-inc/ChromeAlone
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/52dd384fb832f0cd09cb37b9b122f029f9168a9b/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_win_browser_external_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Google\\Chrome\\Extensions.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\update_url") or (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Extensions.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\update_url")
